Key result. \(\sigma\) replaced \(\hat\sigma\):\[
\boxed{t = \frac{\hat\beta_1 - \beta_1}{\widehat{\text{se}}(\hat\beta_1)} \sim t(n-2)}
\]standard error \(\hat\beta_1\) :\[
\widehat{\text{se}}(\hat\beta_1) = \frac{\hat\sigma}{\sqrt{S_{xx}}}
\]distribution Student’s \(t\) \(n - 2\) degrees freedom. \(-2\) comes two parameters estimated (\(\hat\beta_0\), \(\hat\beta_1\)) — one uses one degree freedom.Intuition \(t\) vs \(Z\) distinction. \(Z\)-statistic divide known \(\sigma\); \(t\)-statistic divide estimated \(\hat\sigma\). Estimating \(\sigma\) adds extra uncertainty, making distribution heavier-tailed standard normal. \(n \\infty\), \(\hat\sigma \\sigma\) \(t(n-2) \\mathcal{N}(0,1)\).

hypothesis test asks: data consistent specific claim \(\beta_1\)?Null hypothesis: \(H_0: \beta_1 = \beta_1^0\) (specific value, usually zero)Alternative hypothesis: \(H_1: \beta_1 \neq \beta_1^0\) (two-sided)test statistic \(H_0\):\[
\boxed{t = \frac{\hat\beta_1 - \beta_1^0}{\widehat{\text{se}}(\hat\beta_1)} \sim t(n-2) \text{ } H_0}
\]Decision rule. Fix significance level \(\alpha\) (typically 0.05). Reject \(H_0\) :\[
|t| > c_{\alpha/2}
\]\(c_{\alpha/2}\) \(100(1 - \alpha/2)\)th percentile \(t(n-2)\) distribution. large \(n\), \(c_{0.025} \approx 1.96\).

\(100(1-\alpha)\%\) confidence interval \(\beta_1\) :\[
\boxed{\hat\beta_1 \pm c_{\alpha/2} \cdot \widehat{\text{se}}(\hat\beta_1)}
\]\(c_{\alpha/2} = t_{1-\alpha/2}(n-2)\) critical value \(t(n-2)\) distribution.\(\alpha = 0.05\) large \(n\): \(c_{0.025} \approx 1.96\).Interpretation. repeat sampling procedure many times, approximately \(100(1-\alpha)\%\) resulting intervals contain true \(\beta_1\). single realized interval either contains \(\beta_1\) — probability statement refers procedure, specific interval.

Recall Tutorial 2: \(TSS = ESS + RSS\).\(F\)-statistic compares variation explained model variation remains unexplained, adjusted degrees freedom:\[
\boxed{F = \frac{ESS / k}{RSS / (n - k - 1)}}
\]simple regression (\(k = 1\) regressor):\[
F = \frac{ESS / 1}{RSS / (n-2)} = \frac{ESS}{\hat\sigma^2}
\]\(H_0: \beta_1 = 0\), \(F \sim F(1,\, n-2)\).Decision rule. Reject \(H_0\) \(F > F_\alpha(1, n-2)\), \(\alpha\)-level critical value \(F(1,n-2)\) distribution.

